# What Vercel does NOT need a copy of, on every single deployment.
#
# Deployment Storage is cumulative: every retained deployment keeps its own
# copy of whatever was uploaded. At 134 MB a deployment this project passed
# the 10 GB free allowance around the 75th deploy and reached 63 GB, at which
# point Vercel stops accepting new builds. Roughly 50 MB of that was source
# material the running app never reads.
#
# The test for whether something belongs here: does `prisma generate &&
# next build` read it, or does the server serve it? Everything below fails
# both. `public/` is NOT here — those scenario maps are served.

# Source material for the offline pipeline (`npm run rules:fetch`,
# `rules:extract`, `rules:crosscheck`). The app reads the GENERATED output in
# src/data/generated/, which is committed; it never reads these. The only
# mentions of `data-sources/` under src/ are prose comments citing where a
# value came from, and provenance strings inside the generated JSON.
data-sources/

# Extracted PDF text and working notes from the same pipeline.
scratch/

# Design mockups. Never imported, never served.
stitch_designs/

# Tests and their artefacts. CI runs these; the deployment does not.
e2e/
playwright.config.ts
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Repo documentation.
docs/
